KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 5 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ read through the cast: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
type mismatch on reinterpret_cast
--
The check whether a cast casts away constness compared the pointer-to-array
level by level with the pointer to const int and rejected the cast.  With
CI's GCC 16 snapshot, std::any's _S_manage lost its body
(cpp17_probe_std_any).
